Historical Reference Material
-----------------------------

Files under research/historical_reference/ are retained for research
provenance and historical understanding. Their inclusion does not
automatically relicense them under MIT.

Historical reference material may contain independently authored,
collaborative, experimental, or third-party-derived content. Reuse of an
individual historical file requires review of its provenance, embedded
notices, and any applicable original terms.

Workstation-specific roots in selected historical files were replaced
with the portable PROJECT_ROOT placeholder before public release. The
transformations and original/sanitized hashes are recorded in:

research/inventory/historical_sanitization_manifest.csv

